{"agency_id": "ministry-of-health", "canonical_url": "https://bsky.app/profile/health.govt.nz/post/3miadckrr2s2g", "captured_at": "2026-06-24T22:27:15+00:00", "content": "The Ministry of Health recently hosted the first meeting of the refreshed Pacific Expert Advisory Group (PEAG) — a key step in strengthening how Pacific voices, evidence and community insight shape our work.\n\nWe look forward to working alongside PEAG as they continue this important role.", "content_hash": "e2cdf8ceb2970be7a4c5061660a4f302d4537918a9d5f92417dc1cc22f7413de", "cross_source_ids": {"at_uri": "at://did:plc:nyyntdr37nga3w4lq4kba6la/app.bsky.feed.post/3miadckrr2s2g", "cid": "bafyreibouzvuegjiuj7prbudltk3pskeyf5se2gddrvu36jzer3mrbeimq", "source_id": "ministry-of-health-bluesky-c521eae2"}, "extraction_method": "generic_registered_bluesky_public_api", "media_refs": [{"alt": "Group photo of several people standing and seated around a meeting table in an indoor office setting. Papers and a laptop are visible on the table. Large windows and framed wall art appear in the background. A dark blue banner across the bottom reads ‘Pacific Expert Advisory Group’. Below the banner are the Te Kāwanatanga o Aotearoa New Zealand Government logo and the Ministry of Health Manatū Hauora logo.", "fullsize": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/feed_fullsize/plain/did:plc:nyyntdr37nga3w4lq4kba6la/bafkreih67var2xwvw6gf452nx6sdesmj45247qbmdwf2wzt3mky3kfj4j4", "thumb": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/feed_thumbnail/plain/did:plc:nyyntdr37nga3w4lq4kba6la/bafkreih67var2xwvw6gf452nx6sdesmj45247qbmdwf2wzt3mky3kfj4j4"}], "original_created_at": "2026-03-29T23:44:35.323Z", "raw_path": "historical_archive_raw\\bluesky\\2026-03\\3miadckrr2s2g.json", "record_id": "bluesky:3miadckrr2s2g", "source_account": "health.govt.nz", "source_kind": "social_profile", "source_platform": "bluesky", "source_url": "https://bsky.app/profile/health.govt.nz"}
{"agency_id": "ministry-of-health", "canonical_url": "https://bsky.app/profile/health.govt.nz/post/3mhwh3ahdak2t", "captured_at": "2026-06-24T22:27:15+00:00", "content": "Further information: \nhealthify.nz/health-a-z/f/fetal-anticonvulsant-syndrome-prevention\nwww.facsnz.com\nepilepsy.org.nz/understanding-epilepsy/about-epilepsy\nwww.medsafe.govt.nz/Consumers/educational-material/Epilepsy-medicines-and-pregnancy.pdf", "content_hash": "65de3086dfa3122c909c81b246aa6c279b3dcf396f75e3206de405c16caf2a85", "cross_source_ids": {"at_uri": "at://did:plc:nyyntdr37nga3w4lq4kba6la/app.bsky.feed.post/3mhwh3ahdak2t", "cid": "bafyreidtqkkjpy2xuqj54ysh6j3yx7xi6qzx6rtboegbk4j3izslvics3i", "source_id": "ministry-of-health-bluesky-c521eae2"}, "extraction_method": "generic_registered_bluesky_public_api", "media_refs": [], "original_created_at": "2026-03-26T01:25:27.202Z", "raw_path": "historical_archive_raw\\bluesky\\2026-03\\3mhwh3ahdak2t.json", "record_id": "bluesky:3mhwh3ahdak2t", "source_account": "health.govt.nz", "source_kind": "social_profile", "source_platform": "bluesky", "source_url": "https://bsky.app/profile/health.govt.nz"}
{"agency_id": "ministry-of-health", "canonical_url": "https://bsky.app/profile/health.govt.nz/post/3mhwgvz2bhk2t", "captured_at": "2026-06-24T22:27:15+00:00", "content": "It's Purple Day (international epilepsy awareness day).\nSome anti‑seizure medicines used for seizure disorders can carry risks during pregnancy — early conversations with your healthcare provider matter.\n\nWatch our videos here:\nyoutu.be/Af89KdMSAFQ \nyoutu.be/ulc3vd4flQ0 \nyoutu.be/jcMXcx7d87o", "content_hash": "54f49b1869273431a6cb09f9cf03b3ec1e4c2bd856341950c20904a858535cf1", "cross_source_ids": {"at_uri": "at://did:plc:nyyntdr37nga3w4lq4kba6la/app.bsky.feed.post/3mhwgvz2bhk2t", "cid": "bafyreihfvoyz7w7icjoi4evylqioutmnkt7kbuu4u6gxqr7dwqoiwokipu", "source_id": "ministry-of-health-bluesky-c521eae2"}, "extraction_method": "generic_registered_bluesky_public_api", "media_refs": [{"alt": "Health information graphic titled ‘Foetal Anti‑Convulsant Syndrome (FACS)’. Text states: ‘We estimate 48,000 Kiwis are currently taking anti‑seizure medicines for a range of health needs.’ A photo on the right shows a pregnant abdomen with hands resting on it. A QR code appears with the instruction ‘Scan here to find out more’ leading to Ministry of Health's webpage about FACS. Logos along the bottom include Te Kāwanatanga o Aotearoa New Zealand Government, FACS NZ, Epilepsy New Zealand, and the Ministry of Health Manatū Hauora.", "fullsize": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/feed_fullsize/plain/did:plc:nyyntdr37nga3w4lq4kba6la/bafkreigjuee2u3nq2xpetg5ssju2h7y5k6q6pmyl7cttu3bbkkicudws3y", "thumb": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/feed_thumbnail/plain/did:plc:nyyntdr37nga3w4lq4kba6la/bafkreigjuee2u3nq2xpetg5ssju2h7y5k6q6pmyl7cttu3bbkkicudws3y"}], "original_created_at": "2026-03-26T01:22:31.660Z", "raw_path": "historical_archive_raw\\bluesky\\2026-03\\3mhwgvz2bhk2t.json", "record_id": "bluesky:3mhwgvz2bhk2t", "source_account": "health.govt.nz", "source_kind": "social_profile", "source_platform": "bluesky", "source_url": "https://bsky.app/profile/health.govt.nz"}
{"agency_id": "ministry-of-health", "canonical_url": "https://bsky.app/profile/health.govt.nz/post/3mhh7tf7px22i", "captured_at": "2026-06-24T22:27:15+00:00", "content": "See results from the 2024/25 New Zealand Health Survey: www.health.govt.nz/publications/annual-update-of-key-results-202425-new-zealand-health-survey\nFind out more about oral health: healthify.nz/health-a-z/o/oral-health-taking-care-of-your-teeth", "content_hash": "72bf320f7bb94f15d1f0eca0c968b9827514451808e4d99fa8e131d4788b69b8", "cross_source_ids": {"at_uri": "at://did:plc:nyyntdr37nga3w4lq4kba6la/app.bsky.feed.post/3mhh7tf7px22i", "cid": "bafyreiehent5462scgggwijhrx4n4cq2pxuzkz5sjrelksl7kl5y34p2ze", "source_id": "ministry-of-health-bluesky-c521eae2"}, "extraction_method": "generic_registered_bluesky_public_api", "media_refs": [], "original_created_at": "2026-03-20T00:05:51.492Z", "raw_path": "historical_archive_raw\\bluesky\\2026-03\\3mhh7tf7px22i.json", "record_id": "bluesky:3mhh7tf7px22i", "source_account": "health.govt.nz", "source_kind": "social_profile", "source_platform": "bluesky", "source_url": "https://bsky.app/profile/health.govt.nz"}
{"agency_id": "ministry-of-health", "canonical_url": "https://bsky.app/profile/health.govt.nz/post/3mhh7skp7m22i", "captured_at": "2026-06-24T22:27:15+00:00", "content": "Happy World Oral Health Day! 🦷\nNZ Health Survey 2024/25 highlights:\n• 76.9% of adults report good–excellent oral health\n• 91.6% of children rated good–excellent\n• 2 in 3 brush with fluoride \n• 43% of adults didn’t visit a dental care worker due to cost\n\nMore insights in the survey (link in comments)", "content_hash": "bf12e8d610a06a152a18597a9991dc5bc12f909ab52ac6c20e6cc1163fc66c94", "cross_source_ids": {"at_uri": "at://did:plc:nyyntdr37nga3w4lq4kba6la/app.bsky.feed.post/3mhh7skp7m22i", "cid": "bafyreibm6255c3rclyvgyiaf7wpdpjc52p5zegugglxzmotsprum4zpaom", "source_id": "ministry-of-health-bluesky-c521eae2"}, "extraction_method": "generic_registered_bluesky_public_api", "media_refs": [{"alt": "Square graphic for World Oral Health Day, 20 March 2026. It features two circular infographic charts. The left chart shows 91.6% with text stating that this percentage of children had their oral health rated as good, very good, or excellent by a parent or caregiver. The right chart shows 76.9% with text stating that this percentage of adults reported their oral health to be good, very good, or excellent. A note below states the data comes from the 2024/25 New Zealand Health Survey. At the bottom are the New Zealand Government logo and the Ministry of Health Manatū Hauora logo.", "fullsize": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/feed_fullsize/plain/did:plc:nyyntdr37nga3w4lq4kba6la/bafkreihjqfpti4vizsvkkauugj4tw3ppz66dimgdjbb2aagnkvv6kqpdiu", "thumb": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/feed_thumbnail/plain/did:plc:nyyntdr37nga3w4lq4kba6la/bafkreihjqfpti4vizsvkkauugj4tw3ppz66dimgdjbb2aagnkvv6kqpdiu"}, {"alt": "Square graphic featuring an illustrated smiling tooth character holding a toothbrush. Circular text around the illustration reads: Most people reported having good or excellent oral health. At the bottom are the New Zealand Government logo and the Ministry of Health Manatū Hauora logo", "fullsize": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/feed_fullsize/plain/did:plc:nyyntdr37nga3w4lq4kba6la/bafkreifs4qwc6ppn5hkqbsrdjzkrj5jmgu3jugrc6znf7mkpx7p7gbcc2q", "thumb": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/feed_thumbnail/plain/did:plc:nyyntdr37nga3w4lq4kba6la/bafkreifs4qwc6ppn5hkqbsrdjzkrj5jmgu3jugrc6znf7mkpx7p7gbcc2q"}], "original_created_at": "2026-03-20T00:05:23.687Z", "raw_path": "historical_archive_raw\\bluesky\\2026-03\\3mhh7skp7m22i.json", "record_id": "bluesky:3mhh7skp7m22i", "source_account": "health.govt.nz", "source_kind": "social_profile", "source_platform": "bluesky", "source_url": "https://bsky.app/profile/health.govt.nz"}
